{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And HaShem met with Balaam</b> – Now, for the honor of Israel, this man was elevated to prophesy by the measure of mercy, in the great Name that was revealed to Moses, for until now it is said of him \"And Elohim met with Balaam\" (Numbers 23:4), \"And Elohim came\" (Numbers 22:9). And now he knew that he could not curse them by any means, because by the measure of mercy He would show them grace. For until now, when he would hear by the measure of justice, he would think to find a pretext against them on account of the sin that they had sinned, as in the matter of \"But He turned to be their enemy, He Himself fought against them\" (Isaiah 63:10), or that evil should come upon them from HaShem and they would not escape it by the measure of justice. And this is the meaning of \"And Balaam saw that it was good in the eyes of HaShem to bless Israel\" (Numbers 24:1), for HaShem would also bestow good in the blessing. And the enlightened will understand:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:11.451789687Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}